#: src/development/debugging-crashes.md:3
msgid "Debugging Crashes"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/debugging-crashes.md:5
msgid ""
"When Zed panics or crashes, it sends a message to a sidecar process that "
"inspects the editor's memory and creates a [minidump](https://chromium."
"googlesource.com/breakpad/breakpad/+/master/docs/"
"getting_started_with_breakpad.md#the-minidump-file-format) in `~/Library/"
"Logs/Zed` or `$XDG_DATA_HOME/zed/logs`. You can use this minidump to "
"generate backtraces for all thread stacks."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/debugging-crashes.md:7
msgid ""
"If telemetry is enabled, Zed uploads these reports when you restart the app. "
"Reports are sent to a [Slack channel](https://zed-industries.slack.com/"
"archives/C0977J9MA1Y) and to [Sentry](https://zed-dev.sentry.io/issues) "
"(both are Zed-staff-only)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/debugging-crashes.md:9
msgid ""
"These crash reports include useful data, but they are hard to read without "
"spans or symbol information. You can still analyze them locally by "
"downloading source and an unstripped binary (or separate symbols file) for "
"your Zed release, then running:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/debugging-crashes.md:16
msgid ""
"Alongside the minidump in your logs directory, you should also see a `<uuid>."
"json` file with metadata such as the panic message, span, and system specs."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/debugging-crashes.md:18
msgid "Using a Debugger"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/debugging-crashes.md:20
msgid ""
"If you can reproduce the crash consistently, use a debugger to inspect "
"program state at the crash point."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/debugging-crashes.md:22
msgid ""
"For setup details, see [Using a debugger](./debuggers.md#debugging-panics-"
"and-crashes)."
msgstr ""
